<title>GERMANY: German institutes detail economic forecasts.</title>
<headline>German institutes detail economic forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The six leading German economic research institutes made the following forecasts for pan-German economic indicators in their semiannual report, which was obtained by Reuters early on Tuesday: (real change in percent)</p>
<p>					 1997	 1996	 1995</p>
<p>    GDP				2.5	  1.5	  1.9</p>
<p>    GNP				2.5	  1.0	  1.8</p>
<p>    Private consumption	  1.5	  1.5	  1.8</p>
<p>    Public consumption	   1.0	  2.5	  2.0</p>
<p>    Capital investment	   1.0	 -2.0	  1.5</p>
<p>    Domestic demand		2.0	  1.0	  2.1</p>
<p>    Exports			  6.0	  4.5	  5.9</p>
<p>    Imports			  4.0	  2.5	  6.4</p>
<p>	  -- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
